Threads
-------

* It is a light weight process.

* It is single execution stream in a process which can be independently scheduled by kernel and share the same address space.

* Threads share many attributes are common including data, code and heap section of memory, stack is unique to each thread.

Need of creating threads ?
	
	* Context switch between thread are faster compare to the context switch between the processes.

	(Loading and Unloading process is called context switch).

	* Context switching between two thread then common thing is not loaded and unloaded.

	-> In process PCB is created, In thead TCB is created.

	*  between process to proceess communication need of ipc channel
	   between threads communication no need ot any IPC, 
	   communication between threads is easy than communication between 
	   process.

	* Threads creation is faster than process creation.


Threads will share
	
	. pid, ppid
	
	. controlling terminal

	. code, data, heap

	. open file descriptors
	
	. signal disposition

	. umask

	. resource limits


Threads specific attributes

	. Thread ID
	
	. Signal mask

