	. Thread specific data

	
	Context switch between threads,  only thread specific attributes. switching required not all attributes have less context switch time.

	
	communication between threads is easy (with global variables)




pthread data types
-------------------

1. pthread_t 			:- thread identifier

2. pthread_mutex_t 		:- mutex

3. pthread_mutexattr_t 		:- mutex attribute object

4. pthread_cond_t		:- condition variable

5. pthread_condattr_t 		:- condition variable attribute object

6. pthread_key_t		:- key for thread specific data

7. pthread_once_t 		:- one time initialization

8. pthread_attr_t		:- thread attributes object



pthread_create
-------------

* Creates a new thread

	#include <pthread.h>

	int pthread_create(pthread_t* thread, const* pthread_attr_t* attr, void* (*start_routine) (void*), void* arg);

	compile and link with -pthread

	on success return 0
	
	on error return errno
	
	pthread_t is one data type

	pthread_attr_t is also data type (thread attributes)


pthread_join
------------

* Join with a terminated thread

	int pthread_join (pthread_t thread, void** retval);

	this function waits for the thread specified by thread to terminate. If the thread has already terminated, then pthread_join() return immediately.
	
	
pthread_exit
-----------

* Terminate calling  thread

	void pthread_exit(void* retval);

	the pthread_exit() function terminates the calling threads and returns a value via retval that is available to another thread in the same process thatcause pthread_join().
	
	
		




	
	














































